{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1LbswMD8Q4bpHegjfSL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012d29wn7Kbzd9ANgJr4Adch","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/check_config_change.py","offset":1,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6354,"cache_read_input_tokens":206691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6354},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db09679d-5189-4158-a1d6-4bf6064c9841","uuid":"5614add6-7852-4131-b145-43b8a6f264e7","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:41:27.154Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1LbsiTD5EN3vGJXDbSz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012d29wn7Kbzd9ANgJr4Adch":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/check_config_change.py","offset":1,"limit":60}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012d29wn7Kbzd9ANgJr4Adch","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"PLAN-135 W2 H2 — ConfigChange guard: out-of-band settings.json tamper audit.\n3\t\n4\tCloses the S197 out-of-band-settings-edit observability class. The harness\n5\t``ConfigChange`` event fires when Claude Code's settings change outside the\n6\tnormal in-session flow; this hook RESOLVES the multi-layer settings via the\n7\tshared ``_lib/effective_config`` resolver (the SAME forbidden-keys single\n8\tsource W1 S3 uses), classifies tamper indicators on the SETTINGS-FILE\n9\tsurfaces, and:\n10\t\n11\t  - ALLOWS + audits a benign change (``config_change_observed``, one emit);\n12\t  - ADVISORY-BLOCKS a change that introduces a ``FORBIDDEN_KEYS`` finding\n13\t    (``config_change_forbidden_key``, ONE emit per tamper class), returning\n14\t    a ``{\"decision\": \"block\", \"reason\": ...}`` decision so the operator sees\n15\t    the tamper at the moment of the edit — NOT only at the next boot.\n16\t\n17\t## Coverage boundary (debate R1 — stated honestly in ADR-153 §H2)\n18\t\n19\tH2 is itself a hook. It is:\n20\t  - **disarmed by the very ``disableAllHooks`` it polices** — once that key\n21\t    lands, no further ConfigChange hook runs (a same-session disarm window);\n22\t  - **blind to edits made entirely outside the harness** (a text editor\n23\t    writing settings.local.json on disk fires no ConfigChange event).\n24\t\n25\tNamed compensators (independent channels): the W1 S3 ``/ceo-boot`` Tier-S\n26\tboot tripwires (re-scan the RESOLVED settings + the import-time env snapshot\n27\ton the NEXT boot, catching anything H2's same-session window missed) and the\n28\tW5 O10 OTEL hook-execution witness (an out-of-band record that a hook ran,\n29\tindependent of the hook's own fail-open emit). This hook is a near-real-time\n30\t*detector*, not a *guarantee*.\n31\t\n32\t## Surface scope (deliberately narrower than S3)\n33\t\n34\tH2 polices the SETTINGS FILE surfaces only — a ConfigChange event IS a\n35\tsettings-file change. The ``env`` (process-env) and ``disk`` (hook-census)\n36\ttamper surfaces are S3's at boot and are deliberately NOT block-scoped here\n37\t(``_CONFIG_CHANGE_LAYERS`` = the settings layers + ``other``; census /\n38\tprocess-env findings are filtered out before any block, see\n39\t``_settings_surface_findings``). A settings layer's *own* ``env`` block IS a\n40\tsettings-file change and IS in scope — the resolver classifies it under the\n41\tlayer's own name (``user`` / ``project`` / ``local`` / ``managed``), so it is\n42\tNOT filtered.\n43\t\n44\t## Contract\n45\t\n46\t- ADVISORY by default + fail-open (PLAN-091 S116 doctrine: parse errors /\n47\t  missing files / resolver failure → stderr breadcrumb + emit ``{}``). The\n48\t  ONLY non-empty decision is the forbidden-key BLOCK; every infra condition\n49\t  fails toward ``{}`` (allow), never toward a spurious block.\n50\t- Closed-enum audit only — ``config_change_observed`` /\n51\t  ``config_change_forbidden_key`` are registered in BOTH\n52\t  ``_lib/audit_emit._KNOWN_ACTIONS`` and ``SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md``\n53\t  (v2.43). Both route through their dedicated deny-by-default ``_scrub_``\n54\t  branch; the changed file's PATH/BODY, any settings VALUE, and the\n55\t  effective_config finding DETAIL string NEVER reach the wire.\n56\t- Kill-switch: ``CEO_CONFIG_CHANGE_GUARD=0`` → ``{}`` (no scan, no emit).\n57\t- Stdlib only, Python >= 3.9. ``from __future__ import annotations``,\n58\t  ``typing.Optional`` (no runtime PEP 604).\n59\t\"\"\"\n60\tfrom __future__ import annotations"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db09679d-5189-4158-a1d6-4bf6064c9841","uuid":"d85ca107-fe15-4774-8974-46bda719d0e1","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:41:27.170Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/check_config_change.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"PLAN-135 W2 H2 — ConfigChange guard: out-of-band settings.json tamper audit.\n\nCloses the S197 out-of-band-settings-edit observability class. The harness\n``ConfigChange`` event fires when Claude Code's settings change outside the\nnormal in-session flow; this hook RESOLVES the multi-layer settings via the\nshared ``_lib/effective_config`` resolver (the SAME forbidden-keys single\nsource W1 S3 uses), classifies tamper indicators on the SETTINGS-FILE\nsurfaces, and:\n\n  - ALLOWS + audits a benign change (``config_change_observed``, one emit);\n  - ADVISORY-BLOCKS a change that introduces a ``FORBIDDEN_KEYS`` finding\n    (``config_change_forbidden_key``, ONE emit per tamper class), returning\n    a ``{\"decision\": \"block\", \"reason\": ...}`` decision so the operator sees\n    the tamper at the moment of the edit — NOT only at the next boot.\n\n## Coverage boundary (debate R1 — stated honestly in ADR-153 §H2)\n\nH2 is itself a hook. It is:\n  - **disarmed by the very ``disableAllHooks`` it polices** — once that key\n    lands, no further ConfigChange hook runs (a same-session disarm window);\n  - **blind to edits made entirely outside the harness** (a text editor\n    writing settings.local.json on disk fires no ConfigChange event).\n\nNamed compensators (independent channels): the W1 S3 ``/ceo-boot`` Tier-S\nboot tripwires (re-scan the RESOLVED settings + the import-time env snapshot\non the NEXT boot, catching anything H2's same-session window missed) and the\nW5 O10 OTEL hook-execution witness (an out-of-band record that a hook ran,\nindependent of the hook's own fail-open emit). This hook is a near-real-time\n*detector*, not a *guarantee*.\n\n## Surface scope (deliberately narrower than S3)\n\nH2 polices the SETTINGS FILE surfaces only — a ConfigChange event IS a\nsettings-file change. The ``env`` (process-env) and ``disk`` (hook-census)\ntamper surfaces are S3's at boot and are deliberately NOT block-scoped here\n(``_CONFIG_CHANGE_LAYERS`` = the settings layers + ``other``; census /\nprocess-env findings are filtered out before any block, see\n``_settings_surface_findings``). A settings layer's *own* ``env`` block IS a\nsettings-file change and IS in scope — the resolver classifies it under the\nlayer's own name (``user`` / ``project`` / ``local`` / ``managed``), so it is\nNOT filtered.\n\n## Contract\n\n- ADVISORY by default + fail-open (PLAN-091 S116 doctrine: parse errors /\n  missing files / resolver failure → stderr breadcrumb + emit ``{}``). The\n  ONLY non-empty decision is the forbidden-key BLOCK; every infra condition\n  fails toward ``{}`` (allow), never toward a spurious block.\n- Closed-enum audit only — ``config_change_observed`` /\n  ``config_change_forbidden_key`` are registered in BOTH\n  ``_lib/audit_emit._KNOWN_ACTIONS`` and ``SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md``\n  (v2.43). Both route through their dedicated deny-by-default ``_scrub_``\n  branch; the changed file's PATH/BODY, any settings VALUE, and the\n  effective_config finding DETAIL string NEVER reach the wire.\n- Kill-switch: ``CEO_CONFIG_CHANGE_GUARD=0`` → ``{}`` (no scan, no emit).\n- Stdlib only, Python >= 3.9. ``from __future__ import annotations``,\n  ``typing.Optional`` (no runtime PEP 604).\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":347}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012d29wn7Kbzd9ANgJr4Adch","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1LbswMD8Q4bpHegjfSL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DibHRjjm1nHgpWZTzFVSNg","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/check_config_change.py","offset":240,"limit":80},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6354,"cache_read_input_tokens":206691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6354},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db09679d-5189-4158-a1d6-4bf6064c9841","uuid":"6ed1ae75-51e6-4ee1-90ef-338273a96a67","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:41:29.102Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1LbsiTD5EN3vGJXDbSz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DibHRjjm1nHgpWZTzFVSNg":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/check_config_change.py","offset":240,"limit":80}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DibHRjjm1nHgpWZTzFVSNg","type":"tool_result","content":"240\t        \"on the next boot.\" % (listed or \"unclassified\")\n241\t    )[:_REASON_CAP]\n242\t\n243\t\n244\tdef gate(hook_input: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n245\t    \"\"\"Pure decision function.\n246\t\n247\t    Returns ``{}`` (allow) on every benign / infra path, or\n248\t    ``{\"decision\": \"block\", \"reason\": ...}`` ONLY when a forbidden-key\n249\t    finding is scoped to a settings-file layer. Never raises.\n250\t    \"\"\"\n251\t    if _disabled():\n252\t        return {}\n253\t    cwd = _resolve_cwd(hook_input)\n254\t    session_id = \"\"\n255\t    sid = hook_input.get(\"session_id\")\n256\t    if isinstance(sid, str):\n257\t        session_id = sid[:64]\n258\t    project = \"\"\n259\t    proj = hook_input.get(\"project\")\n260\t    if isinstance(proj, str):\n261\t        project = proj[:128]\n262\t\n263\t    findings = _settings_surface_findings(_classify(cwd))\n264\t\n265\t    # Partition: forbidden-key findings on a block-scope settings layer\n266\t    # (FORBIDDEN_KEYS hits — every classify_tampering finding IS a\n267\t    # FORBIDDEN_KEYS hit by construction) vs. nothing-to-block.\n268\t    forbidden = [\n269\t        f for f in findings\n270\t        if isinstance(f, dict) and f.get(\"layer\") in _BLOCK_SCOPE_LAYERS\n271\t    ]\n272\t\n273\t    if not forbidden:\n274\t        # Benign change (or only env/disk findings, which are S3's surface):\n275\t        # audit one observed event. Layer is best-effort from the highest-\n276\t        # precedence settings layer that exists; default \"other\".\n277\t        _emit_observed(_observed_layer(cwd), session_id, project)\n278\t        return {}\n279\t\n280\t    # ADVISORY-BLOCK path: one audit emit per (tamper_class, layer) pair,\n281\t    # then return a block decision. NEVER degrade a would-be block into a\n282\t    # silent allow on a partial result (the resolver is fail-open; a real\n283\t    # forbidden finding here is authoritative).\n284\t    emitted = set()\n285\t    for finding in forbidden:\n286\t        cls = finding.get(\"class\", \"other\")\n287\t        layer = finding.get(\"layer\", \"other\")\n288\t        key = (cls, layer)\n289\t        if key in emitted:\n290\t            continue\n291\t        emitted.add(key)\n292\t        count = sum(\n293\t            1 for f in forbidden\n294\t            if f.get(\"class\") == cls and f.get(\"layer\") == layer\n295\t        )\n296\t        _emit_forbidden_key(cls, layer, count, session_id, project)\n297\t    return {\"decision\": \"block\", \"reason\": _block_reason(forbidden)}\n298\t\n299\t\n300\tdef _observed_layer(cwd: str) -> str:\n301\t    \"\"\"Best-effort 'which layer was observed' tag for the benign path.\n302\t\n303\t    A ConfigChange event does not always name the changed file; we report the\n304\t    highest-precedence settings layer that exists on disk as a coarse tag\n305\t    (audit-wire closed enum). Fail-open: any failure → ``other``.\n306\t    \"\"\"\n307\t    if not _EFF_AVAILABLE or _eff is None:\n308\t        return \"other\"\n309\t    try:\n310\t        resolved = _eff.resolve_settings(cwd)\n311\t        layers = resolved.get(\"layers\")\n312\t        if not isinstance(layers, list):\n313\t            return \"other\"\n314\t        present = [\n315\t            layer.get(\"name\") for layer in layers\n316\t            if isinstance(layer, dict) and layer.get(\"exists\")\n317\t            and layer.get(\"name\") in _BLOCK_SCOPE_LAYERS\n318\t        ]\n319\t        # LAYER_MERGE_ORDER is lowest→highest precedence; the last present"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db09679d-5189-4158-a1d6-4bf6064c9841","uuid":"8af46911-ed78-4184-923e-823e06eefb88","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:41:29.122Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/check_config_change.py","content":"        \"on the next boot.\" % (listed or \"unclassified\")\n    )[:_REASON_CAP]\n\n\ndef gate(hook_input: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Pure decision function.\n\n    Returns ``{}`` (allow) on every benign / infra path, or\n    ``{\"decision\": \"block\", \"reason\": ...}`` ONLY when a forbidden-key\n    finding is scoped to a settings-file layer. Never raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    if _disabled():\n        return {}\n    cwd = _resolve_cwd(hook_input)\n    session_id = \"\"\n    sid = hook_input.get(\"session_id\")\n    if isinstance(sid, str):\n        session_id = sid[:64]\n    project = \"\"\n    proj = hook_input.get(\"project\")\n    if isinstance(proj, str):\n        project = proj[:128]\n\n    findings = _settings_surface_findings(_classify(cwd))\n\n    # Partition: forbidden-key findings on a block-scope settings layer\n    # (FORBIDDEN_KEYS hits — every classify_tampering finding IS a\n    # FORBIDDEN_KEYS hit by construction) vs. nothing-to-block.\n    forbidden = [\n        f for f in findings\n        if isinstance(f, dict) and f.get(\"layer\") in _BLOCK_SCOPE_LAYERS\n    ]\n\n    if not forbidden:\n        # Benign change (or only env/disk findings, which are S3's surface):\n        # audit one observed event. Layer is best-effort from the highest-\n        # precedence settings layer that exists; default \"other\".\n        _emit_observed(_observed_layer(cwd), session_id, project)\n        return {}\n\n    # ADVISORY-BLOCK path: one audit emit per (tamper_class, layer) pair,\n    # then return a block decision. NEVER degrade a would-be block into a\n    # silent allow on a partial result (the resolver is fail-open; a real\n    # forbidden finding here is authoritative).\n    emitted = set()\n    for finding in forbidden:\n        cls = finding.get(\"class\", \"other\")\n        layer = finding.get(\"layer\", \"other\")\n        key = (cls, layer)\n        if key in emitted:\n            continue\n        emitted.add(key)\n        count = sum(\n            1 for f in forbidden\n            if f.get(\"class\") == cls and f.get(\"layer\") == layer\n        )\n        _emit_forbidden_key(cls, layer, count, session_id, project)\n    return {\"decision\": \"block\", \"reason\": _block_reason(forbidden)}\n\n\ndef _observed_layer(cwd: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort 'which layer was observed' tag for the benign path.\n\n    A ConfigChange event does not always name the changed file; we report the\n    highest-precedence settings layer that exists on disk as a coarse tag\n    (audit-wire closed enum). Fail-open: any failure → ``other``.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _EFF_AVAILABLE or _eff is None:\n        return \"other\"\n    try:\n        resolved = _eff.resolve_settings(cwd)\n        layers = resolved.get(\"layers\")\n        if not isinstance(layers, list):\n            return \"other\"\n        present = [\n            layer.get(\"name\") for layer in layers\n            if isinstance(layer, dict) and layer.get(\"exists\")\n            and layer.get(\"name\") in _BLOCK_SCOPE_LAYERS\n        ]\n        # LAYER_MERGE_ORDER is lowest→highest precedence; the last present","numLines":80,"startLine":240,"totalLines":347}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DibHRjjm1nHgpWZTzFVSNg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1LbswMD8Q4bpHegjfSL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UC8Cx1hxtbUxLDZrz4NXvj","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","offset":300,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6354,"cache_read_input_tokens":206691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6354},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db09679d-5189-4158-a1d6-4bf6064c9841","uuid":"159f5d93-cec1-4902-b2ea-a9946d571b1b","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:41:30.757Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1LbsiTD5EN3vGJXDbSz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UC8Cx1hxtbUxLDZrz4NXvj":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","offset":300,"limit":60}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UC8Cx1hxtbUxLDZrz4NXvj","type":"tool_result","content":"300\t### Fixed — `audit-verify-chain.py --strict-against-counter`\n301\t\n302\t- With the flag, every result maps to a documented exit code with a named\n303\t  reason, one JSON object under `--json`, and no traceback.\n304\t- An absent counter exits 0 and reports `chain_length_source: \"absent\"`.\n305\t  An unreadable counter exits 3.\n306\t- A file and stdin go through one strict decode, and a log that is not a\n307\t  regular file is refused.\n308\t- Without the flag, nothing changes.\n309\t\n310\t### Fixed — three findings of the v1.4.3-rc.1 re-pass\n311\t\n312\t- `diagnose-output-hook.py` can no longer write to the live audit log.\n313\t- `check-audit-real-loss.py` reports a malformed `record_id` instead of\n314\t  crashing.\n315\t- `audit_spool_state.py` and `check-audit-real-loss.py`, both read-only,\n316\t  stop writing bytecode.\n317\t\n318\t### Fixed — harness gate, root `CLAUDE.md` exclusion, plan lifecycle, cost envelope\n319\t\n320\t- `check-active-hooks-executable.py` validates a hook's `type` and\n321\t  `matcher` the way the loader does. A settings path that exists but is\n322\t  not a regular file, and a filesystem error while resolving a hook path,\n323\t  exit 2 with a named error.\n324\t- `check_harness_config.py` turns an exception in that sub-check into a\n325\t  RED finding and keeps its output. Before, it was a degraded warning,\n326\t  which reads as green.\n327\t- A `claudeMdExcludes` value that excludes the root `CLAUDE.md` is\n328\t  classified as settings tamper (`settings_tamper_claude_md_excludes_root`).\n329\t- The harness gate adds an advisory finding, `root_instruction_load`. It\n330\t  reports `root_load_unobservable` unless you pass a complete list of the\n331\t  loaded instruction files with `--instruction-load-evidence`.\n332\t- The plan-lifecycle hook recognizes `PLAN-NNN-FOLLOWUP-<slug>.md` names\n333\t  (`_lib/plan_paths.py`).\n334\t- `check_cost_envelope.py` evaluates nothing, and records no spend, without\n335\t  an absolute `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. Before, it fell back to the current\n336\t  directory.\n337\t\n338\t### Changed — `/ceo-boot` and other files that reach installs\n339\t\n340\t- `/ceo-boot` adds `main_checkout_state`. It is yellow, never red, when the\n341\t  main checkout is off its default branch or on a detached HEAD.\n342\t- The installer copies every top-level `.claude/scripts/*.py`, so six new\n343\t  maintenance helpers reach installs: `_contamination_inventory.py`,\n344\t  `_repin_guard.py`, `_restore_archive.py`, `_subprocess_census.py`,\n345\t  `caller_repo_guard.py` and `check-subprocess-tests.py`. `ceo-restore.sh`\n346\t  uses `_restore_archive.py`.\n347\t\n348\t### Changed — the framework's own CI and release (no installed file changes)\n349\t\n350\t- `scripts/install-npm.sh`, the local packaging check, reads the\n351\t  `npm pack --json` output of npm 12.2 and later, which keys the record by\n352\t  package name. Publishing still pins npm 11.20.0.\n353\t- CI runs on GitHub-hosted runners. The repository variable\n354\t  `VM_CI_ENABLED` is unset, so the self-hosted route that `[1.4.3]`\n355\t  describes is off (measured 2026-11-03).\n356\t- Release automation for the maintainer's Mac: `make mac-sign-merge`,\n357\t  `make mac-cut-rc` and `make mac-cut-ga`.\n358\t- Two red nightly runs on the merge of pull request #7 are cured:\n359\t  - The subprocess census fingerprint pins `ast.dump(..., show_empty=True)`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db09679d-5189-4158-a1d6-4bf6064c9841","uuid":"e125a4ed-e01a-4e9d-b00c-e98df9432b84","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:41:30.781Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"### Fixed — `audit-verify-chain.py --strict-against-counter`\n\n- With the flag, every result maps to a documented exit code with a named\n  reason, one JSON object under `--json`, and no traceback.\n- An absent counter exits 0 and reports `chain_length_source: \"absent\"`.\n  An unreadable counter exits 3.\n- A file and stdin go through one strict decode, and a log that is not a\n  regular file is refused.\n- Without the flag, nothing changes.\n\n### Fixed — three findings of the v1.4.3-rc.1 re-pass\n\n- `diagnose-output-hook.py` can no longer write to the live audit log.\n- `check-audit-real-loss.py` reports a malformed `record_id` instead of\n  crashing.\n- `audit_spool_state.py` and `check-audit-real-loss.py`, both read-only,\n  stop writing bytecode.\n\n### Fixed — harness gate, root `CLAUDE.md` exclusion, plan lifecycle, cost envelope\n\n- `check-active-hooks-executable.py` validates a hook's `type` and\n  `matcher` the way the loader does. A settings path that exists but is\n  not a regular file, and a filesystem error while resolving a hook path,\n  exit 2 with a named error.\n- `check_harness_config.py` turns an exception in that sub-check into a\n  RED finding and keeps its output. Before, it was a degraded warning,\n  which reads as green.\n- A `claudeMdExcludes` value that excludes the root `CLAUDE.md` is\n  classified as settings tamper (`settings_tamper_claude_md_excludes_root`).\n- The harness gate adds an advisory finding, `root_instruction_load`. It\n  reports `root_load_unobservable` unless you pass a complete list of the\n  loaded instruction files with `--instruction-load-evidence`.\n- The plan-lifecycle hook recognizes `PLAN-NNN-FOLLOWUP-<slug>.md` names\n  (`_lib/plan_paths.py`).\n- `check_cost_envelope.py` evaluates nothing, and records no spend, without\n  an absolute `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. Before, it fell back to the current\n  directory.\n\n### Changed — `/ceo-boot` and other files that reach installs\n\n- `/ceo-boot` adds `main_checkout_state`. It is yellow, never red, when the\n  main checkout is off its default branch or on a detached HEAD.\n- The installer copies every top-level `.claude/scripts/*.py`, so six new\n  maintenance helpers reach installs: `_contamination_inventory.py`,\n  `_repin_guard.py`, `_restore_archive.py`, `_subprocess_census.py`,\n  `caller_repo_guard.py` and `check-subprocess-tests.py`. `ceo-restore.sh`\n  uses `_restore_archive.py`.\n\n### Changed — the framework's own CI and release (no installed file changes)\n\n- `scripts/install-npm.sh`, the local packaging check, reads the\n  `npm pack --json` output of npm 12.2 and later, which keys the record by\n  package name. Publishing still pins npm 11.20.0.\n- CI runs on GitHub-hosted runners. The repository variable\n  `VM_CI_ENABLED` is unset, so the self-hosted route that `[1.4.3]`\n  describes is off (measured 2026-11-03).\n- Release automation for the maintainer's Mac: `make mac-sign-merge`,\n  `make mac-cut-rc` and `make mac-cut-ga`.\n- Two red nightly runs on the merge of pull request #7 are cured:\n  - The subprocess census fingerprint pins `ast.dump(..., show_empty=True)`","numLines":60,"startLine":300,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UC8Cx1hxtbUxLDZrz4NXvj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
