{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ChsZ2Whb4TP2q8xyGcyDUb","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t    # only the integer directory DEPTH below the repo root.\n151\t    \"hint_provenance_recorded\",\n152\t    # PLAN-135 W1 S3 — /ceo-boot Tier-S settings/env tamper tripwire\n153\t    # breadcrumb (one emit per detected tamper class). Deny-by-default:\n154\t    # routes through the dedicated _scrub_ branch +\n155\t    # _SETTINGS_TAMPER_DETECTED_ALLOWLIST below, NEVER\n156\t    # _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH\n157\t    # ([[feedback-closed-enum-breadcrumb-must-not-echo-rejected-value]]).\n158\t    # The ONLY caller-supplied fields are `tamper_class` + `layer` (both\n159\t    # closed enums mirroring _lib/effective_config; coerced to \"other\" on\n160\t    # a miss) and integer `finding_count` (clamped 0..99). The tamper\n161\t    # finding DETAIL (endpoint URL / model id / helper path / flag value)\n162\t    # and any env VALUE are NEVER persisted.\n163\t    \"settings_tamper_detected\",\n164\t    # PLAN-135 W2 H2 — ConfigChange guard: a settings-surface config change\n165\t    # was observed and NO forbidden-key finding was scoped to it (allow +\n166\t    # audit path of check_config_change.py). Deny-by-default: routes through\n167\t    # the dedicated _scrub_ branch + _CONFIG_CHANGE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST\n168\t    # below, NEVER _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH\n169\t    # ([[feedback-closed-enum-breadcrumb-must-not-echo-rejected-value]]).\n170\t    # The ONLY caller-supplied field is `layer` (closed enum\n171\t    # user/project/local/managed/other; coerced to \"other\" on a miss). The\n172\t    # changed file's CONTENT, its path text and any key/value are NEVER\n173\t    # persisted.\n174\t    \"config_change_observed\",\n175\t    # PLAN-135 W2 H2 — ConfigChange guard: a forbidden-key finding\n176\t    # (_lib/effective_config.FORBIDDEN_KEYS, the S3/H2 single source) was\n177\t    # scoped to a settings-surface config change → advisory-block