{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KoUJy5GcQJyUpvrL2aDbMx","type":"tool_result","content":"140\t  into `main` with no sentinel and no signature file. Fifteen of them are\n141\t  kernel paths by the kernel list as merged: among them the Bash-guard,\n142\t  canonical-edit, pair-rail, policy and audit-writer hooks, the\n143\t  agent-frontmatter VETO validator, the Codex pin file, the framework's own\n144\t  settings and `validate.yml`. By the list this release restores (Fixed,\n145\t  below), 101 of them are. The merge commit of #7 carries a GPG signature,\n146\t  which is not the signing ceremony. No signed sentinel ratifies those\n147\t  files as of this entry, and nothing in the repository requires one:\n148\t  `main` has no branch protection and no ruleset (measured through the\n149\t  GitHub API on 2026-11-03).\n150\t- **The VETO floor moved from a closed list to family patterns.**\n151\t  - Before, an agent file with `veto_floor: true` had to declare one of\n152\t    four Owner-signed Claude ids.\n153\t  - Now `agent_frontmatter.py` and `escalation_signals.py` also accept any\n154\t    id that matches the families in `_lib/model_currency.py`: Claude Opus\n155\t    majors 4 to 9, `gpt-5` to `gpt-9` and `o3` to `o9`, with numeric and\n156\t    lowercase-word suffixes.\n157\t  - The predicate refuses only the alias `claude-opus-4-1`. It admits ids\n158\t    that the deprecation ledger (`.claude/scripts/model-deprecations.json`)\n159\t    lists as retired or retiring, among them dated Claude Opus 4 and 4.1\n160\t    ids, `gpt-5`, `gpt-5-mini`, `o3`, `o3-mini` and `o4-mini` (probed on\n161\t    2026-11-03).\n162\t  - The docstring of `agent_frontmatter.py` still describes the closed\n163\t    list.\n164\t- **The model allowlist moved to wider family patterns.**\n165\t  - Before, the settings-tamper detector, the agent `model:` check of\n166\t    `validate-governance.sh` and the tier-policy loader accepted only an\n167\t    exact member of a closed list.\n168\t  - Now all three call `is_allowed_model` in `_lib/model_currency.py`\n169\t    (ADR-149 Amendment 4). Besides the listed ids, it admits Claude Opus,\n170\t    Sonnet and Haiku majors 4 to 9, `gpt-5` to `gpt-9`, `o3` to `o9`,\n171\t    `gemini-2` to `gemini-9` and `grok-3` to `grok-9`, with numeric and\n172\t    lowercase-word suffixes.\n173\t  - It refuses only the alias `claude-opus-4-1`, so ids that the\n174\t    deprecation ledger lists as retired pass, among them\n175\t    `claude-sonnet-4-[REDACTED:rg]` and `claude-opus-4-1-[REDACTED:rg]` (probed on\n176\t    2026-11-03).\n177\t  - So `settings_tamper_model_remap`, which `/ceo-boot` reports, no longer\n178\t    flags a model variable (`ANTHROPIC_MODEL`, `ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL`\n179\t    or an `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*` key) set to such an id, for example\n180\t    `gemini-2.5-pro` or `grok-4`, in the environment or in a settings\n181\t    `env` block. An agent file with such a `model:` passes\n182\t    `validate-governance.sh`.\n183\t  - The shipped `availableModels` is unchanged.\n184\t- **The Codex pin moved from an exact payload hash to a version floor.**\n185\t  - Before, `check_pair_rail.py --verify-codex-pin` failed closed on any\n186\t    Codex binary whose payload sha256 differed from the signed manifest,\n187\t    which pins one binary of Codex CLI 0.160.0.\n188\t  - Now a Codex CLI newer than the manifest version passes as\n189\t    `compatible/version_floor_only` when a nearby `@openai/codex`\n190\t    `package.json` declares a stable version at or above 0.160.0\n191\t    (`_lib/cli_currency.py`). The payload's sha256 is still computed and\n192\t    recorded, but on this route a mismatch with the manifest no longer\n193\t    fails.\n194\t  - The release gate follows: `validate-pair-rail-verdict.py` only checks\n195\t    the format of the payload sha of a verdict that declares such a\n196\t    version. Its range check reads the pin file; its payload-hash\n197\t    exemption uses the code constant 0.160.0\n198\t    (`cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR`).\n199\t  - The ADR-182 amendment states the floor as `>=0.160.0`. The pin file\n200\t    reads `>=0.128.0`, with no upper bound: a CI fix in the same pull\n201\t    request lowered it after the amendment.\n202\t  - The operating contract still says the reviewer is pinned by hash, not\n203\t    by range. That no longer describes `main`.\n204\t  - Installs do not receive `.claude/governance/`, so there the pin still\n205\t    resolves as infrastructure and fails open (advisory). That is\n206\t    unchanged.\n207\t  - With `--harness codex`, the installer now prints that it was verified\n208\t    against Codex CLI 0.160.0, while the hook fixtures date from 0.139.0.\n209\t\n210\t### Fixed — the kernel's hard-deny list covers the code the v1.4.4 split moved out of seven kernel entry points, five flat modules that kernel code calls, and the live-adapter package\n211\t\n212\t- The split (PLAN-197) moved the code of seven kernel entry points into\n213\t  helper packages: five hooks (canonical edit, pair rail, agent spawn,\n214\t  audit log and Bash safety) and two hook library modules (policy and\n215\t  audit emit). The same train replaced the plan-path regexes of two\n216\t  kernel files, the plan-lifecycle hook (`check_plan_edit.py`) and the\n217\t  policy preprocessors (`_lib/policy_preprocessors.py`), with the\n218\t  plan-path predicate in `_lib/plan_paths.py`. The kernel's hard-deny\n219\t  list (`check_arbitration_kernel.py`) kept naming only the kernel files,\n220\t  so the 81 files of those packages and the predicate were canonical\n221\t  only: a signed sentinel could unlock them. The list now has a row for\n222\t  each, so that code is hard-deny again, as it was inside the kernel\n223\t  files in v1.4.2.\n224\t- The list also enrolls four modules that kernel code calls, which were\n225\t  canonical only as well: `_lib/model_currency.py`, the VETO-floor\n226\t  predicate that the kernel files `agent_frontmatter.py` and\n227\t  `escalation_signals.py` now call as part of their VETO-floor check; and\n228\t  three modules this train added, `_lib/cli_currency.py` (the Codex\n229\t  payload-pin currency check, called by the pair-rail code),\n230\t  `_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py` (the indirect-execution matcher) and\n231\t  `_lib/bash_indirect_telemetry.py` (its disabled-rail telemetry), both\n232\t  called by the Bash guard's code.\n233\t- The live-adapter package (`_lib/adapters/live/`, 11 files: the ADR-040\n234\t  provider adapters, off by default), which the kernel\n235\t  `_lib/adapters/__init__.py` loads, was canonical only as well, since\n236\t  v1.0.0. It is now enrolled in the kernel, so an edit to it goes through\n237\t  the kernel override like an edit to any kernel file.\n238\t- The list now has one recursive row per package (the seven helper\n239\t  packages and `adapters/live/`), so a file added there later is a kernel"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db09679d-5189-4158-a1d6-4bf6064c9841","uuid":"7fb356d6-a82f-4ff3-bdd0-2111c3d87029","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:42:15.922Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"  into `main` with no sentinel and no signature file. Fifteen of them are\n  kernel paths by the kernel list as merged: among them the Bash-guard,\n  canonical-edit, pair-rail, policy and audit-writer hooks, the\n  agent-frontmatter VETO validator, the Codex pin file, the framework's own\n  settings and `validate.yml`. By the list this release restores (Fixed,\n  below), 101 of them are. The merge commit of #7 carries a GPG signature,\n  which is not the signing ceremony. No signed sentinel ratifies those\n  files as of this entry, and nothing in the repository requires one:\n  `main` has no branch protection and no ruleset (measured through the\n  GitHub API on 2026-11-03).\n- **The VETO floor 