{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1LiBi6nWCngKXfteuDo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fs6qQc2PgcJzneHc2Ni39m","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/adr/ADR-202-kernel-and-hooks-modularization.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1409,"cache_read_input_tokens":245019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1409},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db09679d-5189-4158-a1d6-4bf6064c9841","uuid":"63c1e62a-3b14-4b21-a075-a09e844b0043","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:42:52.685Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1LiBTE66tvartgQcktd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Fs6qQc2PgcJzneHc2Ni39m":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/adr/ADR-202-kernel-and-hooks-modularization.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fs6qQc2PgcJzneHc2Ni39m","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tadr_id: ADR-202\n3\ttitle: Kernel and hooks modularization\n4\tstatus: ACCEPTED\n5\tdate: 2026-11-01\n6\tplan: PLAN-197\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# ADR-202: Kernel and hooks modularization\n10\t\n11\t## Context and decision\n12\t\n13\tEnforcement commit: `027895f1`, `9c020955` (integrated decomposition).\n14\t\n15\tRecord the decomposition already integrated in commits `027895f1` and\n16\t`9c020955`. Existing hook and command paths remain entry points; selected\n17\timplementations move to domain modules. The concrete inventory is in\n18\t[PLAN-197](../plans/PLAN-197-full-monolith-decomposition.md). This is a\n19\tretroactive architecture record, not a claim that every monolith was removed.\n20\t\n21\tCompatibility includes names used by existing callers and tests, including\n22\tprivate patch points where explicitly exported by a component. The component\n23\t`__all__` lists determine what its binder installs; they are not a guarantee\n24\tthat every possible private implementation name is exported. Keep the\n25\toriginal command and hook entry points and their observable contracts.\n26\t\n27\t## Mechanisms and trade-offs\n28\t\n29\t`_lib._audit_emit_parts.install` imports its domain declarations and binds\n30\tfunction code objects to the facade's globals with `FunctionType`; it copies\n31\tmutable declarations for a fresh facade on reload. This preserves call-time\n32\tlookups of patched facade helpers. The `agent_spawn` and `canonical_edit`\n33\tpackages bind their exported functions to the hook globals; the installer\n34\tcensus binder also handles classes and mutable values. The contamination\n35\tscanner binds selected personal-path functions and imports its term scanner.\n36\t`audit-query.py` binds extracted functions and retains named delegates for its\n37\tAST-inspecting read-API guard. These are distinct implementations, not one\n38\tuniversal `sys.modules` proxy: none of these binders replaces its facade in\n39\t`sys.modules` with a proxy.\n40\t\n41\tThe cost is explicit export lists, binding logic, and a requirement to test\n42\tboth the real output and patch points. A plain import/re-export would leave\n43\tfunctions looking up globals in their implementation module, breaking patches\n44\ton the historical facade. Reload and mutable state require particular care.\n45\t\n46\t## AST and integrity boundaries\n47\t\n48\tSource-level consumers must be checked individually. In particular,\n49\t`check-audit-registry-coverage.py` parses `audit_emit.py` for literal\n50\t`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` and `emit_` definitions; moving a function changes what that\n51\tAST can see. Named `audit-query.py` delegates and the functional `audit_emit.py`\n52\t`iter_events` delegate preserve the declarations expected by the read-API\n53\tguard, not the entire pre-decomposition AST. Runtime exports and\n54\tAST-visible declarations are different contracts; neither proves the other.\n55\t\n56\tImport failure policy is owned by each entry point, not by this architectural\n57\trecord. The separate import-integrity work for `check_canonical_edit.py`\n58\taddresses its component failure path; this ADR does not claim equivalent\n59\tfail-closed behavior for every package, nor that imports attest code integrity.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db09679d-5189-4158-a1d6-4bf6064c9841","uuid":"e429ba55-7cfe-40b3-9c5c-b2498bc48fde","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:42:52.707Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/adr/ADR-202-kernel-and-hooks-modularization.md","content":"---\nadr_id: ADR-202\ntitle: Kernel and hooks modularization\nstatus: ACCEPTED\ndate: 2026-11-01\nplan: PLAN-197\n---\n\n# ADR-202: Kernel and hooks modularization\n\n## Context and decision\n\nEnforcement commit: `027895f1`, `9c020955` (integrated decomposition).\n\nRecord the decomposition already integrated in commits `027895f1` and\n`9c020955`. Existing hook and command paths remain entry points; selected\nimplementations move to domain modules. The concrete inventory is in\n[PLAN-197](../plans/PLAN-197-full-monolith-decomposition.md). This is a\nretroactive architecture record, not a claim that every monolith was removed.\n\nCompatibility includes names used by existing callers and tests, including\nprivate patch points where explicitly exported by a component. The component\n`__all__` lists determine what its binder installs; they are not a guarantee\nthat every possible private implementation name is exported. Keep the\noriginal command and hook entry points and their observable contracts.\n\n## Mechanisms and trade-offs\n\n`_lib._audit_emit_parts.install` imports its domain declarations and binds\nfunction code objects to the facade's globals with `FunctionType`; it copies\nmutable declarations for a fresh facade on reload. This preserves call-time\nlookups of patched facade helpers. The `agent_spawn` and `canonical_edit`\npackages bind their exported functions to the hook globals; the installer\ncensus binder also handles classes and mutable values. The contamination\nscanner binds selected personal-path functions and imports its term scanner.\n`audit-query.py` binds extracted functions and retains named delegates for its\nAST-inspecting read-API guard. These are distinct implementations, not one\nuniversal `sys.modules` proxy: none of these binders replaces its facade in\n`sys.modules` with a proxy.\n\nThe cost is explicit export lists, binding logic, and a requirement to test\nboth the real output and patch points. A plain import/re-export would leave\nfunctions looking up globals in their implementation module, breaking patches\non the historical facade. Reload and mutable state require particular care.\n\n## AST and integrity boundaries\n\nSource-level consumers must be checked individually. In particular,\n`check-audit-registry-coverage.py` parses `audit_emit.py` for literal\n`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` and `emit_` definitions; moving a function changes what that\nAST can see. Named `audit-query.py` delegates and the functional `audit_emit.py`\n`iter_events` delegate preserve the declarations expected by the read-API\nguard, not the entire pre-decomposition AST. Runtime exports and\nAST-visible declarations are different contracts; neither proves the other.\n\nImport failure policy is owned by each entry point, not by this architectural\nrecord. The separate import-integrity work for `check_canonical_edit.py`\naddresses its component failure path; this ADR does not claim equivalent\nfail-closed behavior for every package, nor that imports attest code integrity.\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Fs6qQc2PgcJzneHc2Ni39m","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
