{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01REYEQxzGFdRaCnYNcWJ8dz","type":"tool_result","content":"81:AVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET: tuple = (\n82-    # -- VETO floor (base ADR-149 Decision; both members, same order) --\n83-    \"claude-opus-4-8\",    # ADR-142 generation — VETO-floor member\n84-    \"claude-fable-5\",     # running generation — VETO-floor member\n85-    # -- routing tiers (ADR-144 / _lib/model_routing.py _ROUTING_TABLE) --\n86-    \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",  # code_gen / finops tier target\n87-    \"claude-haiku-4-5\",   # file_read / line_audit / digest tier target\n88-    # -- Claude 5 refresh (ADR-181; new ids APPENDED AT END — order is\n89-    #    normative per the Semantics below; any other order needs an\n90-    #    ADR-181 justification) --\n91-    \"claude-opus-5\",      # debate/arch routing + fallback target + floor member\n92-    \"claude-sonnet-5\",    # advisory tier target (ADR-157 member; OQ2 migrate-now)\n93-    # -- Fable 5.1 -- ADR-149 Amendment 2, S338 2026-09-01; APPENDED AT END.\n94-    #    Working-set ONLY: not a floor member, not the fallback, not the\n95-    #    session pin. The legacy claude-fable-5 stays available. --\n--\n112:- `AVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET` is the **availability** statement: the set\n113-  of model ids the harness may select on ANY surface (`/model`, `--model`,\n114-  `ANTHROPIC_MODEL`, subagent `model:` frontmatter, the Agent tool `model`\n115-  parameter, `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL`, advisor, fallback chains). It is\n116-  a tuple, not a set: **order is normative** — the generated settings array\n117-  preserves it, so generation is byte-deterministic.\n118-- Sonnet/Haiku being *available* (ADR-144 tier routing needs them\n119-  selectable for subagent route-down) does **not** make them VETO-eligible.\n120-  VETO eligibility is exclusively `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED` membership, enforced\n121-  by the spawn gate. The two blocks intersect but are never merged.\n122-- `FALLBACK_MODEL_CHAIN` is deliberately length 1 (cap is 3): the primary\n123-  session model is `claude-fable-5` and the sole fallback is\n124-  `claude-opus-5`, a fellow VETO-floor member (ADR-181 refresh; the\n125-  pre-refresh chain pointed at `claude-opus-4-8`). Rationale: (i) an\n126-  availability degradation therefore never drops a session below the VETO\n--\n141:- generate mode emits the JSON fragment from `AVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET`\n142-  (falling back to `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED` members, with a loud stderr note,\n143-  when run against a pre-amendment ADR — the script is live before this\n144-  amendment is applied);\n145-- `--check` mode diffs the resolved settings (project layer +\n146-  `settings.local.json` overlay) against the ADR and exits non-zero on\n147-  drift, including a `fallbackModel` chain that exceeds 3 members or\n148-  escapes the working set.\n149-\n150-Hand-editing the settings arrays without amending this ADR is drift;\n151-`.claude/hooks/tests/test_available_models_mirror.py` (staged with this\n152-amendment) reddens on it.\n153-\n154-### A1.3 Fallback discipline — the three S1b clauses\n155-\n--\n157:`FALLBACK_MODEL_CHAIN` MUST be a member of `AVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET`\n158-(and, while the chain serves governance sessions, of `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED`).\n159-Defense in depth: the harness itself documents that chain elements outside\n160-`availableModels` are dropped when the chain is read and never tried — but\n161-the normative rule is that the chain is AUTHORED inside the floor in the\n162-first place; the harness drop is the backstop, not the policy.\n163-\n164-**(b) All-fallbacks-exhausted = session halts, never silently un-modeled.**\n165-When the primary model and every chain member are unavailable, the turn\n166-MUST fail loudly with an error — the session must never proceed on an\n167-unspecified substitute model or outside the allowlist. The published\n168-harness behavior (unavailable chain elements are skipped; fallback exists\n169-\"instead of failing the request\", implying failure when no element\n170-remains) is consistent with this, but per Doctrine 3 the knob is not\n171-declared adopted until the path is probed:\n--\n245:1. `AVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET` gains `claude-fable-5-1` **at the end**\n246-   (A1.1 order rule — no reorder, no removal). The generated\n247-   `availableModels` mirrors (`.claude/settings.json`,\n248-   `templates/settings/settings.base.json`) follow byte-for-byte via\n249-   `generate-available-models.py`; every INDEPENDENT mirror bound by\n250-   `test_adr149_validator_parity.py` (validate-governance case-arm,\n251-   `tier_policy_cli.VALID_MODEL_IDS`, `smoke-install-parity.sh`\n252-   `ALLOWED_MODELS`) carries the same append in the same patch.\n253-2. `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED` is **unchanged**: Fable 5.1 is selectable, not\n254-   VETO-eligible. Routes (a)/(b) — floor membership with or without\n255-   migrating the six `agents/*.md` pins — stay open as a FUTURE amendment\n256-   that the Owner may ratify after measuring the 5.1 verdict quality;\n257-   nothing here pre-empts it.\n258-3. `FALLBACK_MODEL_CHAIN` is **unchanged** (`claude-opus-5`).\n259-4. The session-default `model` pin stays `claude-opus-5` in all three\n--\n391:1. `AVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET` gains `claude-opus-5-5` **at the end**\n392-   (A1.1 order rule — no reorder, no removal). The generated\n393-   `availableModels` mirrors follow via `generate-available-models.py`;\n394-   every independent mirror bound by `test_adr149_validator_parity.py`\n395-   carries the same append in the same patch.\n396-2. `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED` — the base Decision block and\n397-   `agent_frontmatter.VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED`, set-equal by test — gains\n398-   `claude-opus-5-5`. Membership makes the id ELIGIBLE to render a VETO; it\n399-   migrates no agent file: every `veto_floor: true` agent file keeps its\n400-   `model: claude-fable-5` pin. (A2.2 item 2 states a count of those files\n401-   that does not match the tree it