{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T3vZQnodoQo4NTvz6UBxP3","type":"tool_result","content":"28\t\n29\tReplace every exact-equality model pin in the VETO-floor enforcement chain\n30\twith membership in ONE Owner-signed allowlist:\n31\t\n32\t```python\n33\tVETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED: frozenset = frozenset({\n34\t    \"claude-opus-4-8\",   # ADR-142 generation — remains valid (additive)\n35\t    \"claude-fable-5\",    # S225/PLAN-134 W0 — the running generation (ceiling pin)\n36\t    \"claude-opus-5\",     # ADR-181 (PLAN-163 T1.3, OQ1=b) — Claude 5 Opus joins the floor\n37\t    \"claude-opus-5-5\",   # ADR-149 Amendment 3 (S357, PLAN-193) — Opus 5.5 joins the floor\n38\t})\n39\t```\n40\t\n41\t- `agent_frontmatter.py` owns the canonical constant; the spawn gate checks\n42\t  membership. `validate-governance.sh`, `escalation_signals.py` (family\n43\t  prefixes derived from the allowlist members), and `tier_policy_cli`\n44\t  mirror it per the existing defense-in-depth doctrine (independent\n45\t  literals + frozen SHA stay — they pin the ALLOWLIST now, not one ID).\n46\t- Tests assert membership, not equality (`test_veto_floor_bijection.py`\n47\t  variant-A companion patch).\n48\t\n49\t## Consequences\n50\t\n51\t- A future generation bump = add ONE id to the allowlist + mirrors + rerun\n52\t  the SHA regen — a data change inside the ADR-052 ceremony, not a\n53\t  redesign. Removal of an id remains an Owner-only act (never automatic).\n54\t- Downgrade protection is preserved: anything outside the allowlist\n55\t  (haiku/sonnet/unknown) still blocks the spawn loudly.\n56\t- The allowlist is the trust statement: its content is ratified at GPG\n57\t  ceremony; CI enforces consistency across the 4 mirror sites.\n58\t- Explicitly NOT decided here: which generation the 5 VETO agents pin\n59\t  (variant A vs B — an Owner choice recorded at the same ceremony, per\n60\t  E1-F3); routing economics (PLAN-134 W3); non-VETO tier tables (ADR-067).\n61\t\n62\t## Amendment 1 (PLAN-135 W1 — availableModels working set + fallback discipline)\n63\t\n64\t> Authored S231 under PLAN-135 W1 (unit s1); staged in\n65\t> `.claude/plans/PLAN-135/staged/w1/`; effective only when the Owner\n66\t> ceremony applies the W1 bundle. Harvest provenance: HARVEST-REPORT S1;\n67\t> debate R1 clauses (b)/(c) from `architect/round-1/security-engineer.md`.\n68\t> Settings-key reality verified against the published Claude Code docs\n69\t> (`settings` + `model-config` pages, fetched 2026-06-12): `availableModels`\n70\t> (array of model ids/aliases) and `fallbackModel` (array, chain capped at 3)\n71\t> are REAL harness keys; `enforceAvailableModels` is NOT a key (speculative\n72\t> name from debate R1 — do not ship it).\n73\t\n74\t### A1.1 Two blocks, two meanings (machine-parseable)\n75\t\n76\tThe base Decision's `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED` block above is **unchanged** — it\n77\tremains the spawn-gate trust statement: the only models permitted to render\n78\ta VETO verdict. This amendment ADDS a **distinct, wider** block:\n79\t\n80\t```python\n81\tAVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET: tuple = (\n82\t    # -- VETO floor (base ADR-149 Decision; both members, same order) --\n83\t    \"claude-opus-4-8\",    # ADR-142 generation — VETO-floor member\n84\t    \"claude-fable-5\",     # running generation — VETO-floor member\n85\t    # -- routing tiers (ADR-144 / _lib/model_routing.py _ROUTING_TABLE) --\n86\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",  # code_gen / finops tier target\n87\t    \"claude-haiku-4-5\",   # file_read / line_audit / digest tier target\n88\t    # -- Claude 5 refresh (ADR-181; new ids APPENDED AT END — order is\n89\t    #    normative per the Semantics below; any other order needs an\n90\t    #    ADR-181 justification) --\n91\t    \"claude-opus-5\",      # debate/arch routing + fallback target + floor member\n92\t    \"claude-sonnet-5\",    # advisory tier target (ADR-157 member; OQ2 migrate-now)\n93\t    # -- Fable 5.1 -- ADR-149 Amendment 2, S338 2026-09-01; APPENDED AT END.\n94\t    #    Working-set ONLY: not a floor member, not the fallback, not the\n95\t    #    session pin. The legacy claude-fable-5 stays available. --\n96\t    \"claude-fable-5-1\",   # Mythos-class flagship 5.1; dateless id per the models overview\n97\t    # -- Opus 5.5 -- ADR-149 Amendment 3, S357 2026-09-22; APPENDED AT END.\n98\t    #    Working set AND VETO floor; the session-default pin. The\n99\t    #    fallback stays claude-opus-5, which stays available. --\n100\t    \"claude-opus-5-5\",    # Opus 5.5; dateless id per the models overview\n101\t)\n102\t```\n103\t\n104\t```python\n105\tFALLBACK_MODEL_CHAIN: tuple = (\n106\t    \"claude-opus-5\",      # VETO-floor member (ADR-181 refresh, OQ1=b) — degradation never leaves the floor\n107\t)\n108\t```\n109\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db09679d-5189-4158-a1d6-4bf6064c9841","uuid":"7592da47-d704-4c98-aa45-55cc8d93ed9e","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:43:56.369Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/adr/ADR-149-model-id-allowlist.md","content":"\nReplace every exact-equality model pin in the VETO-floor enforcement chain\nwith membership in ONE Owner-signed allowlist:\n\n```python\nVETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED: frozenset = frozenset({\n    \"claude-opus-4-8\",   # ADR-142 generation — remains valid (additive)\n    \"claude-fable-5\",    # S225/PLAN-134 W0 — the running generation (ceiling pin)\n    \"claude-opus-5\",     # ADR-181 (PLAN-163 T1.3, OQ1=b) — Claude 5 Opus joins the floor\n    \"claude-opus-5-5\",   # ADR-149 Amendment 3 (S357, PLAN-193) — Opus 5.5 joins the floor\n})\n```\n\n- `agent_frontmatter.py` owns the canonical constant; the spawn gate checks\n  membership. `validate-governance.sh`, `escalation_signals.py` (family\n  prefixes derived from the allowlist members), and `tier_policy_cli`\n  mirror it per the existing defense-in-depth doctrine (independent\n  literals + frozen SHA stay — they pin the ALLOWLIST now, not one ID).\n- Tests assert membership, not equality (`test_veto_floor_bijection.py`\n  variant-A companion patch).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- A future generation bump = add ONE id to the allowlist + mirrors + rerun\n  the SHA regen — a data change inside the ADR-052 ceremony, not a\n  redesign. Removal of an id remains an Owner-only act (never automatic).\n- Downgrade protection is preserved: anything outside the allowlist\n  (haiku/sonnet/unknown) still blocks the spawn loudly.\n- The allowlist is the trust statement: its content is ratified at GPG\n  ceremony; CI enforces consistency across the 4 mirror sites.\n- Explicitly NOT decided here: which generation the 5 VETO agents pin\n  (variant A vs B — an Owner choice recorded at the same ceremony, per\n  E1-F3); routing economics (PLAN-134 W3); non-VETO tier tables (ADR-067).\n\n## Amendment 1 (PLAN-135 W1 — availableModels working set + fallback discipline)\n\n> Authored S231 under PLAN-135 W1 (unit s1); staged in\n> `.claude/plans/PLAN-135/staged/w1/`; effective only when the Owner\n> ceremony applies the W1 bundle. Harvest provenance: HARVEST-REPORT S1;\n> debate R1 clauses (b)/(c) from `architect/round-1/security-engineer.md`.\n> Settings-key reality verified against the published Claude Code docs\n> (`settings` + `model-config` pages, fetched 2026-06-12): `availableModels`\n> (array of model ids/aliases) and `fallbackModel` (array, chain capped at 3)\n> are REAL harness keys; `enforceAvailableModels` is NOT a key (speculative\n> name from debate R1 — do not ship it).\n\n### A1.1 Two blocks, two meanings (machine-parseable)\n\nThe base Decision's `VETO_FLOOR_ALLOWED` block above is **unchanged** — it\nremains the spawn-gate trust statement: the only models permitted to render\na VETO verdict. This amendment ADDS a **distinct, wider** block:\n\n```python\nAVAILABLE_MODELS_WORKING_SET: tuple = (\n    # -- VETO floor (base ADR-149 Decision; both members, same order) --\n    \"claude-opus-4-8\",    # ADR-142 generation — VETO-floor member\n    \"claude-fable-5\",     # running generation — VETO-floor member\n    # -- routing tiers (ADR-144 / _lib/model_routing.py _ROUTING_TABLE) --\n    \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",  # code_gen / finops tier target\n    \"claude-haiku-4-5\",   # file_read / line_audit / digest tier target\n    # -- Claude 5 refresh (ADR-181; new ids APPENDED AT END — order is\n    #    normative per the Semantics below; any other order needs an\n    #    ADR-181 justification) --\n    \"claude-opus-5\",      # debate/arch routing + fallback target + floor member\n    \"claude-sonnet-5\",    # advisory tier target (ADR-157 member; OQ2 migrate-now)\n    # -- Fable 5.1 -- ADR-149 Amendment 2, S338 2026-09-01; APPENDED AT END.\n    #    Working-set ONLY: not a floor member, not the fallback, not the\n    #    session pin. The legacy claude-fable-5 stays available. --\n    \"claude-fable-5-1\",   # Mythos-class flagship 5.1; dateless id per the models overview\n    # -- Opus 5.5 -- ADR-149 Amendment 3, S357 2026-09-22; APPENDED AT END.\n    #    Working set AND VETO floor; the session-default pin. The\n    #    fallback stays claude-opus-5, which stays available. --\n    \"claude-opus-5-5\",    # Opus 5.5; dateless id per the models overview\n)\n```\n\n```python\nFALLBACK_MODEL_CHAIN: tuple = (\n    \"claude-opus-5\",      # VETO-floor member (ADR-181 refresh, OQ1=b) — degradation never leaves the floor\n)\n```\n","numLines":82,"startLine":28,"totalLines":797}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01T3vZQnodoQo4NTvz6UBxP3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
