{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HC49HgyGQo4iy4d5qUPj9C","type":"tool_result","content":"14-- **D1 — no `bypassPermissions`, anywhere.** The only mode `on` ever\n15-  writes is `acceptEdits`, and `off` restores only values from the\n16-  closed set `_RESTORABLE_MODES` — which NEVER includes\n17-  `bypassPermissions` (NM-01). `bypassPermissions` in ANY settings layer\n18:  trips `TAMPER_PERMISSION_BYPASS` (`_lib/effective_config.py`) and turns\n19-  `/ceo-boot` red by design; the honest escape valve is an explicit,\n20-  ephemeral `claude --permission-mode bypassPermissions` session.\n21-- **D2 — single-writer via ceremony prerequisite P1.** A deny rule for\n22-  Edit/Write on `.claude/settings.local.json` (sentinel ceremony, blocks\n--\n24-  the only writer of the overlay. This script does not and cannot\n25-  enforce P1 itself; it relies on it for the escalation-ladder closure.\n26-- **D3 — the boot banner derives from the resolver, not the marker.**\n27-  The marker/snapshot file is decoration + restore-state only. `status`\n28:  reconciles marker vs `_lib.effective_config.resolve_settings()` and\n29-  REPORTS disagreement instead of picking a side.\n30-\n31-## State model (W0 decisions — fixed, do not revisit)\n32-\n--\n260-# NM-01 / NF-01 / NF-02 — closed set of modes `off` may restore. Derived,\n261-# with exactly two exclusions, both load-bearing:\n262-#\n263-# - `bypassPermissions` (D1): present in ANY settings layer it trips\n264:#   `TAMPER_PERMISSION_BYPASS` (`_lib/effective_config.py`) and turns\n265-#   `/ceo-boot` red by design. night-mode must never be the thing that\n266-#   writes it back — not even under the name \"restoring\".\n267-# - `NIGHT_MODE` (`acceptEdits`, NF-01): cmd_on's desync normalization\n268-#   guarantees that a HEALTHY marker never carries night-mode's own value\n--\n324-# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n325-\n326-# Bind extracted implementation to this module global namespace.\n327-_hooks_dir = str(REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\")\n328:if _hooks_dir not in sys.path:\n329:    sys.path.insert(0, _hooks_dir)\n330-from _lib._night_mode_parts import install as _install_parts\n331-_install_parts(globals(), (\"helpers\", \"toggles\"))\n332-\n333-def _local_layer(resolved: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n--\n340-def cmd_status(root: Path) -> int:\n341-    \"\"\"Reconcile marker vs resolver and REPORT disagreement (D3 + contract 5).\n342-\n343-    Read-only; always exits 0. The posture line derives from\n344:    `_lib.effective_config.resolve_settings()` — the same resolver the\n345-    tamper tripwires use — never from the marker alone.\n346-\n347-    NF-06 (round-4): this command RUNS `_validate_marker` and renders its\n348-    verdict. It used to print `host=` / `ts=` raw and reconcile a marker it\n--\n355-    and every rendered line is collapsed with `_one_line` so no future echo\n356-    can forge a record either.\n357-    \"\"\"\n358-    hooks_dir = str(REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"hooks\")\n359:    if hooks_dir not in sys.path:\n360:        sys.path.insert(0, hooks_dir)\n361:    from _lib import effective_config  # noqa: E402\n362-\n363:    resolved = effective_config.resolve_settings(str(root))\n364-    effective = resolved.get(\"effective\") or {}\n365-    permissions = effective.get(\"permissions\")\n366-    eff_mode = permissions.get(\"defaultMode\") if isinstance(permissions, dict) else None\n367-    eff_layer = (resolved.get(\"sources\") or {}).get(\"permissions\", \"(none)\")\n368-\n369-    lines: List[str] = [\"## night-mode status\"]\n370-    lines.append(\n371-        \"effective permissions.defaultMode: {0} \"\n372:        \"(layer: {1}; resolver: _lib.effective_config)\".format(\n373-            # NF-06: bounded — the winning value can come from the overlay.\n374-            _bounded_repr(eff_mode), eff_layer,\n375-        )\n376-    )\n--\n587-            # import its own lock is not re