{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WGC1tcbQRYf5QVNqVVvdbF","type":"tool_result","content":"270\t    # The overlay decides the NEXT session's permission mode and the\n271\t    # marker's prev_value is restored into it by night-mode off —\n272\t    # posture-write by proxy. No ceremony ever tool-edits these\n273\t    # (night-mode.py writes them as a process), so they sit at kernel\n274\t    # tier: no sentinel can grant a tool write. The WRITER script is\n275\t    # deliberately canonical-tier only (future ceremonies must be able\n276\t    # to evolve it under sentinel).\n277\t    \".claude/settings.local.json\",\n278\t    \".claude/state/night-mode.json\",\n279\t    # PLAN162_FIX_3 (PLAN-162 findings #3 + #8, consensus C10) — the two\n280\t    # files the guards themselves TRUST, previously guarded by NEITHER\n281\t    # rail (verified on HEAD: canonical=False, kernel=False for both):\n282\t    #\n283\t    #   1. the ADR-121 sentinel signer REGISTRY — the identity root\n284\t    #      `check_canonical_edit._sentinel_grants_path` consults on the\n285\t    #      dual signer rail. Unguarded, an ordinary Edit silently disarms\n286\t    #      half the signer check, asymmetric with the legacy\n287\t    #      `.claude/sentinel-signers.txt` which HAS been kernel-guarded\n288\t    #      since ADR-116.\n289\t    #   2. the policy hash-pin drift MANIFEST — it pins the policy files\n290\t    #      that are themselves guarded; leaving the pinner rewritable\n291\t    #      makes the pin decorative (\"pin the pinner\").\n292\t    #\n293\t    # Both are KERNEL tier (no sentinel escape) precisely because a\n294\t    # sentinel that grants an edit to the signer registry could authorize\n295\t    # its own future signer. Deliberately NOT paired with an\n296\t    # \"absence ⇒ fail-closed\" inversion (C10): that would need a\n297\t    # definition of \"expected\" which is itself editable, and would make\n298\t    # DELETING a file the way to choose the posture.\n299\t    \".claude/security/sentinel-signers-registry.yaml\",\n300\t    \".claude/policies/.drift-manifest.json\",\n301\t    # KERNEL-DECOMPOSITION (v1.4.4 train, merge 888e9e6c). These rows\n302\t    # cover the code the v1.4.4 split moved out of seven kernel facades,\n303\t    # the plan-path predicate the train put in place of regexes in two\n304\t    # kernel files, and the modules listed below that kernel code calls.\n305\t    #   - Seven facades moved their code into helper packages. One recursive\n306\t    #     row per package makes that code HARD-DENY again, as it was inside\n307\t    #     the facades in v1.4.2, and a file added there later is HARD-DENY\n308\t    #     too (the federation-dir precedent above).\n309\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/**/*\",  # check_canonical_edit.py\n310\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/agent_spawn/**/*\",  # check_agent_spawn.py\n311\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_policy_parts/**/*\",  # _lib/policy.py\n312\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*\",  # _lib/audit_emit.py\n313\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_log_parts/**/*\",  # audit_log.py\n314\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/**/*\",  # check_bash_safety.py\n315\t    \".claude/hooks/_lib/_pair_rail_parts/**/*\",  # check_pair_rail.py\n316\t    #   - Five flat modules that kernel code calls:\n317\t    #     plan_paths.py — the plan-path predicate (is_plan_path,\n318\t    #       plan_id_from_path) that replaces the plan-path regexes the train\n319\t    #       removed from check_plan_edit.py and policy_preprocessors.py; it\n320\t    #       is HARD-DENY again, as those regexes were in v1.4.2;\n321\t    #     model_currency.py — is_veto_floor_model(), the VETO-floor predicate\n322\t    #       that kernel files now call as part of their VETO-floor check\n323\t    #       (the F-01-03 demotion check above rides on it);\n324\t    #     cli_currency.py, bash_indirect_guard.py, bash_indirect_telemetry.py\n325\t    #       — each added